-- 2-propanol. Atoms: 0 the central carbon with hydrogen 1, 2 the oxygen with hydrogen 3, 4 the first
-- methyl carbon with hydrogens 5 to 7, 8 the second with hydrogens 9 to 11. The two methyls are
-- enantiotopic, by the same argument as glycerol's two arms: the central carbon carries a hydrogen, a
-- hydroxyl and two identical groups, so exchanging the groups is a reflection.
num-ipa-obs : List Nat
num-ipa-obs = cons 1 (cons 5 (cons 6 (cons 7 (cons 9 (cons 10 (cons 11 nil))))))
